Summary: Install stub AMD and NVIDIA DLLs in 64-bit prefixes, for D3DMetal
Category: graphics
Kind: feature
Origin: crossover
From: CrossOver 26.3.0 CW HACK 22435, the wine.inf part (loader/wine.inf.in)
Source: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-26.3.0.tar.gz (sources/wine/loader/wine.inf.in)
CW-Hack: 22435
Upstream: no
Why: Have wineboot put fake (stub) atidxx64.dll, nvapi64.dll and nvngx.dll
 in a 64-bit prefix's system32. CX's comment says only "for D3DMetal";
 presumably D3DMetal, or games running on it, check that these AMD/NVIDIA
 DLLs exist. No builtin DLLs have those names, so setupapi writes generic
 fake DLLs.
Programs: none known
Evidence: Sikarugir 10.0_8: its share/wine/wine.inf has these lines with this
 comment; it is the only difference in share/.
Port: to 10.0: CX 25.1.1 lacks this; CX 26.3's lines added to 10.0's [FakeDllsWin64] unchanged.
Applies to: wine 10.0 (macfixes, after 0049)
Status: not yet built (2026-11-15).

diff --git a/loader/wine.inf.in b/loader/wine.inf.in
index e3426b7..6386816 100644
--- a/loader/wine.inf.in
+++ b/loader/wine.inf.in
@@ -2160,6 +2160,10 @@ HKLM,%CurrentVersion%\Telephony\Country List\998,"SameAreaRule",,"G"
 [FakeDllsWin64]
 10,twain_64,sane.ds
 10,twain_64,gphoto2.ds
+; CW HACK 22435: fake DLLs for D3DMetal
+11,,atidxx64.dll,*
+11,,nvapi64.dll,*
+11,,nvngx.dll,*
 
 ; Wow64-only fake dlls
 [FakeDllsWow64]
